+# Review: team documents "Why Wharton chose Laura" and "Client Profile: Laura Gao" (2026-09-27)
+
+Both documents were written by the team from public sources before cross-checking the official case. The originals
+are kept out of this public repo because they contain personal details not needed for strategy. This file keeps only
+strategy-relevant conclusions. Assistant review; the team decides.
+
+## Supported by the case / official criteria (keep)
+- Client trend: from personal wealth goals to funding community infrastructure over years (Ayoola 2024-25 -> Barwin
+  2025-26 -> Gao 2026-27). Laura's case adds co-sponsors and scored credibility under uncertainty.
+- Wharton wants risk management, funding reliability and honest communication of uncertainty, not return-chasing
+  (evaluation criteria: Portfolio Analysis; Creativity and Presentation).
+- Willingness vs capacity: her career already carries concentrated risk (publishing, speaking, licensing), so the
+  portfolio should not add correlated risk. In the case this bites through the 2028 $150k deposit.
+- Human-capital hedge: mild underweight of publishing/media exposure in the growth sleeve; name book-challenge and
+  AI-disruption risks to the 2028 deposit (present the AI trade-off as her choice, not ours).
+- Low-cost, transparent, explainable instruments (her data/finance background).
+- Narrative frames from her own work: "strong foundations for messy roots"; "lessons for falling" = plan for
+  drawdowns. Use as framing carried by analysis, not decoration. Avoid tokenism.
+- Write plainly and honestly; ranges and probabilities with stated models, not point forecasts.
+
+## Conflicts with the official case (do not use)
+- The facility contribution is NOT a dated fixed liability; it has no preset amount (case p.3). The fixed liability is
+  the ten $50k payments 2033-2042.
+- No income-gap cash buffer: living expenses are covered outside the portfolio and there are no withdrawals before
+  2033 (case p.2).
+- "Residency" = a creative residency in Taiwan she establishes (case p.2-3), not where she lives.
+- The case names no ESG/values preference or exclusions: screens are at most a question to put to Laura.
+- Teaching (CCA) income is not part of the case; the 2028 deposit comes from publishing advances, speaking,
+  licensing and other ventures (case p.2).
+
+## Unverified (sources blocked in this environment)
+Career details, festival figures, CCA-Vanderbilt, client list before 2023-24. Verify before citing.
